WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:07.620
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Arrow we got our first official look at

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.620
the Suicide Squad.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:13.049
The writers have big plans for them that include
the battle against Deathstroke this season

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:15.019
and stuff happening in season 3.

00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:17.650
I’ll talk about all that and what’s going
on in the next couple of episodes.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.650
I’ve even got some cool details on the Flash
crossover that’s coming.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.970
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Arrow and Flash videos every week.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.260
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.460
Tomorrow I’ll be posting a Q&amp;A video, so
be sure to write any questions you want me

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.590
to include in the comments.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.399
So now let’s talk about our Top 5 moments
from the episode, then I’ll do some of my

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:37.000
favorite references to the comic books and
my review.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.360
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.870
Here we go, Number 5 - Oliver’s Awful Home
Movies.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:48.670
In keeping with the theme of the episode Oliver
steps into the killbox that is Slade’s office.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.450
Felicity dropped the “suicide” reference.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.680
Just tying it to the Suicide Squad A-story.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:59.490
I loved how you could just tell Slade was
setting the table for Oliver so to speak.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.610
A buffet of death with an appetizer of awful
memories.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:08.210
It’s almost like this is Hannibal and Oliver
is Will Graham, being framed for murder by

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.609
Hannibal Lecter played by Slade.

00:01:11.609 --> 00:01:12.899
Shows within shows.

00:01:12.899 --> 00:01:15.960
I always love scenes where characters sit
and watch movies.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.049
In this case there wasn’t really any subtext
to the Shado movie, it was just Slade making

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:21.659
Oliver think about her.

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:26.159
I wonder how many other awful home movies
Slade has collected.

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:29.799
He strikes me as the kind of obsessive person
who would also just sit there and watch Shado

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:31.340
on a loop all night.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.469
When he wasn’t busy watching Oliver’s
house on a loop.

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:38.990
Number 4 - Diggle and Deadshot’s heart to
heart.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.369
Not an action scene, but full of action.

00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:44.670
This was a really good moment for anyone who
hasn’t read the comics.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.740
Essentially of all the Suicide Squad members,
Deadshot is the closest to being a good person.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.579
Or a good person who does really bad things.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:02:00.380
I loved that he said the drone strike was
his way out.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.999
I think they were misleading us a little.

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:07.939
He probably expected to escape at the last
second and just let them believe he was dead.

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:11.790
A character that proficient doesn’t lose
the will to live just because he’s working

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.900
with Amanda Waller.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.700
Maybe she just sucks the life out you with
those cold stares.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.120
And that’s her superpower.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:23.489
Diggle’s arc in the episode was recognizing
the grey area, which is what the Suicide Squad

00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:24.900
is all about.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.730
Just like the Thunderbolts in the Marvel universe,
I don’t think they ever really get rehabilitated.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:29.860
They’ll always be villains.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.290
But that’s why it’s so much cooler when
you see them team up with heroes.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.680
And in case you missed it, that last scene
with Amanda Waller and Oliver is a teaser

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.680
for a future episode.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.610
They’ll be helping Oliver take down Slade.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.549
Number 3 - We’ve been tracking a new player.

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:45.180
We’re calling him Deathstroke.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:50.870
It’s a little crazy that Amanda Waller with
all her resources, doesn’t know Slade is

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.659
the Deathstroke they’ve been tracking.

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:57.060
They kind of buried the lead a little, but
in that moment, Waller basically gave Slade

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.060
his callsign.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:03.030
I know Billy Winters wore the mask in season
1, but did any of the characters ever use

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.109
the name Deathstroke?

00:03:04.109 --> 00:03:06.030
I can’t remember.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:09.189
This whole exchange with Waller is really
just an awesome teaser for Oliver co-opting

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.609
the Squad to take down Slade in a future episode.

00:03:11.609 --> 00:03:14.800
We don’t know when they’re going to be
back, I would guess that it’s going to either

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.969
be in episode 18 called Deathstroke or in
one of the final episodes.

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:23.450
There will be 23 total, but we only have details
up to episode 20.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.079
The other thing I thought was really interesting
about this ARGUS scene was that it gives you

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:33.900
the sense that something even bigger than
the Oliver VS Slade battle is coming.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:42.209
Like that’s not even the biggest moment
that’s coming this season.

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:46.999
I talked about how Manu Bennett was teasing
Ra’s Al Ghul in a previous video.

00:03:46.999 --> 00:03:50.760
I can’t quite remember which one it was,
but I have a playlist link at the end of this

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:51.760
video.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.640
So you can scan through all my Arrow Season
2 stuff if you want the details on that.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.640
Long story short.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.590
The conflict between Slade and Oliver is going
to cause so much damage that Ra’s Al Ghul

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.249
will come to deal with it.

00:04:02.249 --> 00:04:04.499
Number 2 - Meet Task Force X

00:04:04.499 --> 00:04:06.749
So this is the suicide squad.

00:04:06.749 --> 00:04:12.609
But Task Force X is a big comic book reference
to an organization consisting of Checkmate,

00:04:12.609 --> 00:04:14.390
The Suicide Squad and Argent.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:20.220
It was created to fill the void left by the
Justice Society when they retired.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.950
This all happened back in the 80s.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:26.520
The thing that really got me excited about
them was that because the show has made it

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.520
official.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.970
They can start developing the team and use
them even more in season 3.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:35.230
The showrunners said that they have this mutli-season
approach to developing those characters and

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.230
the team.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.510
Jut like they’re doing with The Birds of
Prey starting in next week’s episode.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:43.700
Think of this episode as the teaser for future
Suicide Squad episodes.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.190
And if they’re really successful, they might
even spin off Suicide Squad like they’re

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.190
doing for The Flash.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:53.060
That’s a long ways off, so don’t plan
on seeing any more Arrow spinoffs for a long

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.060
time.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.870
The Flash still hasn’t even been given a
series order yet.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:05:00.500
But there is a lot more Suicide Squad coming,
later this season and next season.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:06.230
and my number 1 moment - Do you cuties need
help, I’m a trained therapist.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:11.140
And with just a few lines, we get one of the
biggest teasers all season long.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:16.860
Meet Harley Quinn, core member of The Suicide
Squad and a backdoor to the Batman Universe.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.720
Don’t expect the Joker anytime soon or Nightwing
for that matter.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.570
But it’s possible that we’ll actually
be seeing her character the next time the

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:25.540
Suicide Squad is featured this season.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:30.130
The funny thing is that they listed her in
the credits as “Deranged Team Member”.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:33.600
Which means they didn’t want to do an official
reveal yet.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.620
Why that is, I have no idea.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.130
But a lot of people thought Cassidy Alexa
was actually playing her.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:42.390
But Tara Strong was listed as the voice in
the credits.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:46.630
It’s possible that they just dubbed her
over Cassidy Alexa.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.590
Tara Strong has done the voice for Harley
in all the Batman Arkham video games for the

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:51.680
last couple of years.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.930
So they really did go to the source for authenticity.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:59.940
It would have been funny if they had used
the original voice from the animated series,

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:03.280
but I can totally understand them wanting
to use someone who is currently voicing the

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:10.500
character.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:14.730
In one of my earlier videos I talked about
Chekov’s Gun.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:19.490
It’s the idea that you never include something
unless you’re going to pay it off later

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:20.490
in the story.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:22.710
Never make a promise you don’t intend to
keep.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:26.690
Since they gave us Harley Quinn’s voice,
it’s like promising us that she’ll be

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.210
on the show at some point.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:31.680
So we will get to see her full on, soon.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.270
No confirmation on which episode though.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.310
But bet on it being the next time the Suicide
Squad is featured.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:37.620
Now it’s your turn though, let me know what
you’re favorite moment was.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.750
Harley Quinn, I know.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.120
We’re all thinking the same thing.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.620
So here’s a couple really big comic book
references and funny things from the episode

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:45.730
before I do my review.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.150
First, Felicity had a stalker in college.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:50.420
This was just hilarious.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:56.300
2 - Diggle’s Booty Call, during which we
find out Amanda Waller has also used the Argus

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:59.170
suite for her own Booty Calls in the past.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:02.160
This is even funnier if you know the comic
book version of her character.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:06.490
3 - The khandaq name drop is a reference to
Black Adam.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:10.830
They haven’t introduced the idea of Magic
on Arrow in a big way, but this makes it seem

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.110
like they will in a distant season.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:15.050
Like season 5 or beyond.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.030
Billy Batson cameo anyone?

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:22.030
4 - Ben Browder Backdoor Cameo again as Ted
Gaynor from the comics.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:27.000
5 - Another shout out to Lyla Michaels Harbinger
character from the comics.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:32.470
Lyla in the comics was given huge superpowers
by the Monitor during the big Crisis on Infinite

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.880
Earths storyline back in the 80s.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.430
and last one number 6 - Several shout outs
to Deadshot’s daughter Zoe Lawton from the

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:43.020
comics.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:47.300
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, just
because it was so much fun and they were able

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.630
to use all these characters without the story
collapsing under the weight.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.960
It was a really good dark Arrow story.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:58.410
You have all these villains so naturally it
made sense for Oliver to be really dark.The

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:03.180
writers are doing a really good job of bringing
all the different storylines this season together

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.760
for this big Deathstroke battle.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.940
But remember, that’s not even the biggest
thing that’s going to happen.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.560
There’s the threat of Ra’s Al Ghul, just
casting a shadow over Slade.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:15.960
That’s why Arrow has become one of my favorite
shows this year.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.150
It just keeps unvieling bigger and bigger
threats.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:23.040
Right now Agents of SHIELD has the clairvoyant.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:28.420
But in order to match Arrow, they’d have
to reveal an A-List supervillain behind the

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.420
clairvoyant.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:32.940
Let me know what you thought of the episode
and remember, Birds of Prey next week.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.849
Be sure to subscribe to get my video.

00:08:34.849 --> 00:08:37.500
My Q&amp;A video for this will post tomorrow.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.680
So leave me all your questions.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:44.260
Right now click here to learn more about The
Flash and Click here to learn all about Avengers

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:45.260
2.

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:46.470
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:47.030
High Fives!

